  "title": "Closing the Seams in African Care Delivery",
  "summary": "Healthcare in many African markets does not fail only because care is unavailable. It often fails because care is hard to complete. Patients may find a provider, but booking is inconsistent. They may see a clinician, but next steps are unclear. Results arrive late or get lost. Payments feel opaque. Follow-ups depend on memory, paper,...",
